---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ScreenshotSlot from '../../components/ScreenshotSlot.astro';
import FeatureExplorer from '../../components/FeatureExplorer.astro';
import SettingsPreview from '../../components/SettingsPreview.astro';
import WorkshopLinks from '../../components/WorkshopLinks.astro';
import { harmonyUrl } from '../../data/workshop';
import art from '../../assets/projects/ai-improve.png';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout title="AI Improve" description="AI Improve makes Cities: Skylines 1 vehicles, services and citizens react to real conditions: congestion, crowded platforms, nearby fires and spare capacity." path="ai-improve/" active="mods">
	<section class="hero page-wrap">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Mod 01 · Available on the Workshop</p>
			<h1>AI Improve</h1>
			<p class="hero-lead">Smarter decisions for the vehicles, services and citizens of your city. Every behaviour has its own switch, so you choose exactly what changes.</p>
			<div class="status-strip"><span class="tag">Requires Harmony</span><span class="tag">25 switchable features</span><span class="tag">9 languages</span></div>
			<WorkshopLinks mod="ai-improve" />
		</div>
		<figure class="hero-art"><Image src={art} alt="AI Improve artwork" widths={[560, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 45vw" format="webp" quality={78} loading="eager" /><figcaption class="art-note">Project artwork · not a gameplay screenshot</figcaption></figure>
	</section>

	<nav class="subnav page-wrap" aria-label="AI Improve guide"><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/overview/'}>Guide</a><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/features/'}>All features</a><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/settings/'}>Settings</a><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/in-game/'}>Using it in game</a><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/compatibility/'}>Compatibility</a><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/faq/'}>FAQ</a></nav>

	<section class="section soft">
		<div class="page-wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Why it exists</p>
			<h2>The city should notice what is happening.</h2>
			<p class="section-intro">In the base game, a car keeps its route while the road ahead is jammed, trains crowd onto one platform while another sits empty, and several fire trucks answer one small fire. AI Improve adds that awareness one behaviour at a time.</p>
			<div class="highlight-grid">
				<article><h3>Reacts to congestion</h3><p>Cars, taxis, trucks, buses, metro and intercity trains reconsider their route when the way ahead is jammed.</p></article>
				<article><h3>Uses free capacity</h3><p>Platforms, airport gates, helicopter pads and harbour docks are assigned by how busy they actually are.</p></article>
				<article><h3>Sends the right response</h3><p>Fire, garbage and hearse vehicles check nearby needs first, and fire responses per building are capped.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="interactive-section"><div class="page-wrap"><p class="section-label">Feature browser</p><h2>See what each feature does.</h2><p>Pick a category, then a feature, to see an illustration of the behaviour and whether it starts on or off.</p><FeatureExplorer locale="en" /></div></section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack">
				<p class="eyebrow">Settings</p>
				<h2>Every switch, before you subscribe.</h2>
				<p>This mirrors the mod’s options page in the Content Manager, with the same sections and defaults. Open a section to see its switches and advanced values. It is a web demonstration only and changes nothing in your game.</p>
				<a class="text-link" href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/settings/'}>Read what each setting does →</a>
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Options page in the Content Manager" description="The General section with language, logging and advanced tuning, followed by one section per category." />
			</div>
			<div class="demo-shell"><SettingsPreview locale="en" /></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section soft">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack">
				<p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p>
				<h2>Plays well with other mods.</h2>
				<p>AI Improve needs <a href={harmonyUrl}>Harmony</a>. Where another mod already handles the same job, it steps aside instead of fighting it: the stop-timing features pause while Improved Public Transport or Express Bus Services is installed, and when Transfer Manager CE runs fire dispatch, AI Improve leaves the choice of fire to it and only keeps the per-building cap. It never changes how many passengers a vehicle carries.</p>
				<p>One known limit: aircraft rerouting while taxiing does not trigger yet, because measured taxiway congestion never reaches the level it reacts to.</p>
				<div class="link-list"><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/compatibility/'}>Compatibility details →</a><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-improve/faq/'}>FAQ and how to report a problem →</a></div>
			</div>
			<div class="screenshot-stack">
				<ScreenshotSlot title="In-game panel" description="The AI Improve panel opened from the UnifiedUI toolbar, with quick switches for each feature." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="A feature at work" description="Traffic rerouting around a jam, or trains spread across free platforms at a busy station." />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
